@* The problem's locator, rendered in normal flow wherever the host places it —
   sibling of XgidLabel, bound at the same one site (SPEC-quiz-view.md §4). The
   file name is middle-truncated to a capped width, because the row it sits in
   is board budget; the untruncated name is what a screen reader is given and
   what a hover reveals. Renders nothing when the record locates nothing (see
   the code-behind). *@
@if (HasFileName || HasCoordinates)
{
    <div class="problem-locator" role="group" aria-label="@LocatorLabel">
        @if (HasFileName)
        {
            @* The accessible name is the record's file name verbatim, extension
               and all — the thing the reader goes looking for on disk. The
               visible twin beside it is the shortened form, hidden from the
               accessibility tree so the name is not announced twice. *@
            <span class="visually-hidden">@SourceFile</span>
            <span class="problem-locator-file" aria-hidden="true" title="@SourceFile">@DisplayFileName</span>
        }
        @if (HasCoordinates)
        {
            <span class="problem-locator-where">@WhereText</span>
        }
    </div>
}
